WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.925
Note: This video is part of your Module 1 classroom

00:07.925 --> 00:10.800
instruction. The visit and tour of the mine,

00:10.800 --> 00:13.737
required by Part 48, is a separate,

00:13.737 --> 00:15.100
in-person step.

00:18.412 --> 00:21.125
Welcome to Boonesboro Quarry. This video walks

00:21.125 --> 00:23.662
you through the site before your in-person tour,

00:23.662 --> 00:26.337
so you know where things are and how we work here.

00:26.337 --> 00:29.087
Boonesboro is an underground mine. It produces

00:29.087 --> 00:32.312
crushed stone, from base and DGA to clean stone

00:32.312 --> 00:33.300
sizes.

00:34.414 --> 00:36.564
Every shift starts at the tag board.

00:36.564 --> 00:39.064
Hang your tag when you arrive, and take it down

00:39.064 --> 00:41.714
when you leave. That's how we know who's on site

00:41.714 --> 00:44.901
in an emergency. Visitors and contractors use a

00:44.901 --> 00:46.139
separate check-in.

00:49.497 --> 00:51.622
Here's how traffic moves on this site.

00:51.622 --> 00:54.135
Haul trucks run between the underground mine and

00:54.135 --> 00:56.959
the plant; road trucks come through the scale.

00:56.959 --> 00:59.297
Pedestrians stay on the marked walkways,

00:59.297 --> 01:02.059
and nobody walks on a haul road. The speed limit

01:02.059 --> 01:06.097
is 15 miles per hour on the surface and 25 underground.

01:06.097 --> 01:08.434
Traffic is two-way and keeps right,

01:08.434 --> 01:10.359
and haul trucks have the right of way.

01:10.359 --> 01:12.934
In a pickup, call the haul truck on the radio before

01:12.934 --> 01:15.809
you approach it. Watch for overhead power lines

01:15.809 --> 01:19.347
on Level 1. Remember: make contact with an operator

01:19.347 --> 01:21.747
and get an answer back before you approach any

01:21.747 --> 01:22.660
equipment.

01:23.786 --> 01:26.599
We communicate by radio; your supervisor will give

01:26.599 --> 01:29.624
you the channels and call words. Warning signals

01:29.624 --> 01:33.036
here include the horn and backup alarms on equipment,

01:33.036 --> 01:35.299
the plant start-up horn, and the blast warning

01:35.299 --> 01:36.111
signal.

01:39.457 --> 01:42.219
The basic cycle here is drill, blast,

01:42.219 --> 01:46.044
load, haul and crush. Drilling and blasting are

01:46.044 --> 01:48.894
done by our own Allen crew. Underground,

01:48.894 --> 01:52.357
the rooms here are about 35 by 45 feet.

01:52.357 --> 01:54.519
You'll see the mining method for yourself on your

01:54.519 --> 01:57.482
mine tour. Never work near a highwall or with your

01:57.482 --> 01:58.532
back to one.

01:59.659 --> 02:01.759
The plant is where you'll find crushers,

02:01.759 --> 02:04.834
screens and conveyors; stay on walkways and out

02:04.834 --> 02:07.521
of guarded areas. The shop has its own rules for

02:07.521 --> 02:10.371
lockout and hot work. The scale house is where

02:10.371 --> 02:12.709
trucks are weighed before they leave the pit.

02:16.024 --> 02:18.637
In an emergency, go to the gathering point:

02:18.637 --> 02:22.449
Tag Board, or Outback behind the mine at 22 North.

02:23.628 --> 02:27.066
For a serious injury or fire, call 911.

02:27.066 --> 02:30.766
Madison County E911 dispatches all three.

02:30.766 --> 02:35.466
Tell them: Boonesboro Quarry, 2591 Boonesborough Rd,

02:35.466 --> 02:37.978
Richmond, and where the injured person is:

02:37.978 --> 02:41.903
underground, pit, plant, scale or shop.

02:41.903 --> 02:44.115
Then call the mine office so someone meets the

02:44.115 --> 02:47.291
ambulance at the gate. Nearby hospitals are Baptist

02:47.291 --> 02:50.066
Health Richmond, Clark Regional Medical Center,

02:50.066 --> 02:52.141
Baptist Health Lexington ER.

02:53.260 --> 02:55.710
Your in-person mine tour is the next,

02:55.710 --> 02:58.172
separate step. Ask questions about anything you

02:58.172 --> 02:58.910
see.

03:00.022 --> 03:03.184
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

03:03.184 --> 03:04.685
override this video.
